<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_DATA_SYNC" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS" />
    <!-- Optional envelope relay to desktop local API (adb reverse loopback). -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />

    <!--
      Package visibility (API 30+): queryBroadcastReceivers() only returns
      packages this app can see. Declaring the agent text-input broadcast actions
      here is what makes the (A)I Sees A5 survey possible without asking for
      QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES, which is Play-policy restricted and far broader than we
      need. Only receivers matching these exact actions become visible.
    -->
    <!--
      Package visibility (Android 11 / API 30+).

      Without an entry here, getPackageInfo() throws NameNotFoundException for an
      app we cannot see, which is indistinguishable from "not installed". That made
      every attestation Unreadable, so a registry full of pinned certificates could
      never verify anything — the check would be present and permanently useless.

      Each <package> below must match an entry in policies/known-apps.yaml. A
      deployment that pins additional apps has to add them here too; there is no way
      to make this list dynamic, which is the cost of not requesting the
      QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES restricted permission (Play Store review treats that as a
      last resort, and a guardrail that can enumerate every installed app is a
      privacy problem of its own).
    -->
    <queries>
        <intent>
            <action android:name="ADB_INPUT_B64" />
        </intent>
        <intent>
            <action android:name="ADB_INPUT_TEXT" />
        </intent>
        <package android:name="com.sankuai.meituan" />
        <package android:name="com.autonavi.minimap" />
        <package android:name="com.tencent.mm" />
        <package android:name="me.ele" />
        <package android:name="com.stripe.android" />
        <package android:name="com.example.legacypos" />
        <!--
          AgentScan §3.6 needs the *opposite* visibility from §3.5, and the difference is
          load-bearing.

          §3.5 asks "is the app claiming to be WeChat really WeChat", which only ever concerns a
          *registered* package — the six above. §3.6 asks "is this unregistered app dressed as
          WeChat", and the clone is by construction **not** in that list. With only the six
          <package> entries, `getApplicationLabel`/`getApplicationIcon` throw
          NameNotFoundException for every clone on API 30+, `AppFace` returns nulls, the envelope
          carries no app_label or icon_dhash, and `check_app_lookalike` returns None. The
          mechanism would be inert on device for the one attack it exists to catch — Kotlin
          computing a value the engine never receives, which is this project's most-repeated
          defect.

          A MAIN/LAUNCHER intent query makes every *launchable* app visible. That is the widest
          thing this companion asks for, and the trade is stated rather than buried: it is enough
          to enumerate the user's launcher, which is a privacy cost. It is still narrower than
          QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES — services, providers and headless packages stay invisible — and it
          is not a restricted permission, so it does not need a Play Store declaration. A clone
          must be launchable to be the app the agent opens, so this is exactly the set §3.6 needs
          and no more.

          See docs/app-lookalike.md, "Package visibility is the whole mechanism".
        -->
        <intent>
            <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
            <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
        </intent>
    </queries>

    <application
        android:name=".AgentGuardApplication"
        android:networkSecurityConfig="@xml/network_security_config"
        android:allowBackup="false"
        android:label="AgentGuard Companion"
        android:supportsRtl="true"
        android:theme="@android:style/Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar">

        <activity
            android:name=".MainActivity"
            android:exported="true">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>

        <service
            android:name=".GuardAccessibilityService"
            android:exported="false"
            android:permission="android.permission.BIND_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICE">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.accessibilityservice.AccessibilityService" />
            </intent-filter>
            <meta-data
                android:name="android.accessibilityservice"
                android:resource="@xml/accessibility_service_config" />
        </service>

        <service
            android:name=".GuardForegroundService"
            android:exported="false"
            android:foregroundServiceType="dataSync" />
    </application>
</manifest>
